== P-1 TO P-6, P-8 AND P-9 RE-RUN, AND THE HARNESS WAS RED BEFORE THE PRODUCT
== 23 September 2026, local scratch cluster, nothing touched the live project

THE HEADLINE. The nine-probe harness had been broken since 09:32 the same
morning and nobody had re-run it. Migration 20260923093233 added
`escrows.opened_by` and made `escrow_fund_from_wallet_as` write it. The
harness builds a MINIMAL copy of `escrows` by hand, that copy has no such
column, and the harness lifts the CURRENT function text out of the migration
files. So every probe that funds an escrow died on the insert:

  ERROR:  column "opened_by" of relation "escrows" does not exist
  QUERY:  insert into public.escrows (payer_id, payee_id, listing_id, purpose,
          amount_minor, opened_by)
  CONTEXT: PL/pgSQL function escrow_fund_from_wallet_as(...) line 42

TEN OF ELEVEN FAILED. That is the correct behaviour and the harness is not at
fault for reporting it: it did not report a pass. What is at fault is that a
suite whose whole purpose is the sentence "no naira moves until all nine
probes pass" can go red for a day with nothing saying so.

AND ONE OF THE ELEVEN PASSED WITH THE ESCROW DOOR COMPLETELY BROKEN.
P-2 (withdrawal_first) reads PASS in the summary below. Its assertion is that
exactly one of the withdrawal and the escrow commits the balance, that both
sessions SPOKE rather than raised, and that the payer ends at zero. With the
withdrawal going first it takes the balance, and the escrow door is then
refused `insufficient` by the spendable check BEFORE it ever reaches the
insert that would have failed. Every condition is met. The word `insufficient`
is the expected answer whether the door behind it is sound or unusable.

  -- A:
       WITHDRAWAL ok
  -- B:
       ESCROW insufficient
     ok_answers=1 committing_entries=1 payer_spendable=0
     BOTH-ANSWERED: yes. ESCROW and WITHDRAWAL both spoke.
  == P-2 (withdrawal_first): PASS.

That is the day's blind light. `both_answered` was added to stop a probe
counting a crash as a refusal, and it works in the escrow_first direction,
which correctly read FAIL with "BOTH-ANSWERED: no". In the other direction the
escrow leg is refused for a REAL reason upstream of the fault, so the control
has nothing to catch. THE PASS IS TRUE AND IT IS NOT EVIDENCE ABOUT THE
ESCROW DOOR.

-- THE SUMMARY, VERBATIM.

== SUMMARY
   P-1                FAIL Expected A ok and B insufficient with exactly one hold. Read the two session outputs above.
   P-2 (escrow_first) FAIL Both paths took the balance, neither did, or one of them never ran.
   P-2 (withdrawal_first) PASS Exactly one of the two committed the balance. The other was refused and nothing was moved.
   P-3a (pot)         FAIL The pot and the escrow both reached the same naira, neither did, or one of them never ran.
   P-3b (transfer)    FAIL The transfer and the escrow both reached the same naira, neither did, or one of them never ran.
   P-4                FAIL A double settle produced something other than exactly one credit and one audit row.
   P-5 (sweeper first) FAIL The race produced state=ERROR:  invalid input syntax for type uuid: ""
   P-5 (dispute first) FAIL The race produced state=ERROR:  invalid input syntax for type uuid: ""
   P-6                FAIL A retry on one reference moved money twice, or answered with something other than duplicate.
   P-8                FAIL An illegal transition was not refused by the trigger.
   P-9                FAIL The float identity did not hold across a lifecycle mix.

== RESULT: FAIL. 10 of 11 local probes failed.
